# research/data: downloaded archives, extracted third-party datasets and anything derived
# from them in bulk are NOT committed (licences forbid redistribution and/or they are large).
# Everything here can be recreated with research/scripts/download_datasets.py and the
# build/convert scripts (pinned commits + hash manifests make the result reproducible).
#
# Committed: this file, README.md, manifests/ (hashes of every downloaded file), splits/,
# reports/ (validation summaries), and the small manifest/summary/failure tables of the
# corpora we derive ourselves (Mutopia, Beringer). The derived PIG-format FingeringFiles
# are regenerated by the build scripts and stay local.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
!manifests/
!manifests/**
!splits/
!splits/**
!reports/
!reports/**
!mutopia_fingering/
mutopia_fingering/*
!mutopia_fingering/manifest.csv
!mutopia_fingering/manifest.json
!mutopia_fingering/summary.json
!mutopia_fingering/failures.csv
!beringer_fingering/
beringer_fingering/*
!beringer_fingering/manifest.csv
!beringer_fingering/summary.json
# never commit these, wherever they appear
**/.download_complete.json
**/.locks/
**/_build/
**/_downloads/
**/__pycache__/
